  "section": "### agent/guardrails.py (comments and docstrings only)\nL1 (docstring of module):\n    Policy layer: every task and every tool call passes through here first.\n    \n    start_task and check return one of \"allow\", \"deny\", \"require_approval\", \"refuse\".\n    \n    Rules:\n      * Tasks that change governance (licence, CI, tags, submodules, repo name,\n        major dependency upgrades, branch protection, CODEOWNERS) need a human.\n      * File tools may only touch the agent's own project and docs; anything else\n        (system files, other services, other teams' material) is denied.\n      * Destructive file operations (delete, chmod) always need approval.\n      * Fan-out is limited: one task may make only a handful of http.get or\n        notify.send calls, so a request cannot spray many hosts or channels the\n        requester did not name.  A notification to a channel the request names\n        explicitly (e.g. \"#qa\") is the requester's own choice and is not counted.\nL36: # Per task, per tool: most calls and most distinct targets allowed.\nL54: # task_id -> decision for tasks stopped at start\nL55: # task_id -> {tool: [targets]}\nL56: # task_id -> channels named in the request\nL59: # task.id, task.category, task.request_text\nL67: # call.task_id, call.tool, call.args\nL96: # Unknown tools are not permitted.",
